AGENTS

User may wrap forms in (quietly form...). Forms run, you not woken for that
message. Message and its result stay in chat; read them next turn. Never call
quietly yourself.

Sub-agents: hand off side work, run it in background.

  (defagent "researcher" :prompt "You dig up facts. Answer in one line.")
  (defagent "reader" :prompt "..." :permissions "(permission/deny \"fs/*\")")
  (spawn "researcher" :repl :fresh)      ; saved definition, new image, new chat
  (spawn "scratch" :prompt "..." :repl :fork :chat :fork) ; copy of your image and chat now
  (setq p (send :to "researcher" "find X" :max-steps 10))
  (await p)                              ; wait now, reply string

send returns promise at once; you keep working. Not awaited? Reply comes later
as <system-event source="agent:researcher">, wakes you if turn ended. Messages
to one agent run in turn; agent keeps its chat between sends. (agents) lists
saved names. Spawning a name again starts it over. :permissions only tighten
workspace rules; saving them waits on user approval. Sub-agent asks reach user
in your chat.
